cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NERVES, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "NERVES: Normalized Entropy Representation of Voxelwise Eigenvalue Spectra"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-04-24
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19738588
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/TravisBeckwith/NERVES
abstract: >
  NERVES is an end-to-end pipeline for computing Normalized Diffusion Entropy
  (NDE) maps from diffusion-weighted MRI data. NDE quantifies the Shannon entropy
  of the diffusion tensor eigenvalue spectrum. It is a function of FA and
  tensor mode, so any added value over FA is exploratory and unvalidated.
  NDE is a tensor-eigenvalue summary measure; it is related to, but not the same
  estimator as, the model-free diffusion entropy of Fozouni et al. (2013).
authors:
